Cell["\<\
k and boundaryDirection are two- or three-component vectors. Cells are \
grouped by the norm of their displacement projected onto boundaryDirection, \
then ordered by displacement norm within each group.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1090745269,ExpressionUUID->"d25d30e2-ba72-2c4c-848c-a4e713eb214e"],

Cell["\<\
The implementation accepts cell associations of lengths 4, 7, 8, 10, 15, or \
19. Their arrangement must provide the representative cells required by the \
grouped indexing.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->342846563,ExpressionUUID->"c81cea11-70b4-ed43-b2b7-326f099949d1"],

Cell["\<\
For lengths 4, 8, or 10, returns {leadOnsiteBloch, leadIntercellBloch}. For \
lengths 7, 15, or 19, returns {{leadOnsiteBloch, leadIntercellBloch}, \
{surfaceOnsiteBloch, surfaceLeadCouplingBloch}}.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1130089920,ExpressionUUID->"057f1786-f5b2-e540-bd3b-7da98cae906a"],

Cell["\<\
The partial Bloch sums use HBlochFull, so all in-plane directed hoppings \
needed by each cell group must be represented explicitly.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1602351461,ExpressionUUID->"1216d0e0-dccc-d248-a10a-a3e020fc189f"]
}, Closed]],

